        "content": "I have all the information. Let me solve the problem.\n\n**Problem 16:** In △ABC, AB=3, BC=2√3, cosB=√3/3.\n(1) Find cosA.\n(2) D is on ray BA beyond A, DE∥BC, AE⊥AC, DE=√6, find CE.\n\n**Part (1):** By law of cosines, AC² = AB² + BC² − 2·AB·BC·cosB = 9 + 12 − 2·3·2√3·(√3/3) = 21 − 12 = 9, so AC = 3.\n\nThen cosA = (AB² + AC² − BC²)/(2·AB·AC) = (9 + 9 − 12)/(2·3·3) = 6/18 = 1/3.\n\n**Part (2):** Set coordinates. Let A = (0,0), B = (3,0). Since cosB = √3/3, sinB = √6/3. C = B + BC·(cos(π−B), sin(π−B))... Let me place C using angle at B: C = (3 − 2√3·cosB, 2√3·sinB) = (3 − 2√3·(√3/3), 2√3·(√6/3)) = (3 − 2, 2√2) = (1, 2√2).\n\nCheck AC = √(1+8) = 3 ✓.\n\nD on ray BA beyond A: D = (−t, 0), t>0. DE∥BC, so E = D + s·(C−B) = (−t,0) + s·(−2, 2√2) = (−t−2s, 2√2 s).\n\nAE⊥AC: AE·AC = 0. AE = (−t−2s, 2√2 s), AC = (1, 2√2). So (−t−2s) + 2√2·2√2 s = −t−2s+8s = −t+6s = 0 → t = 6s.\n\nDE = √6: DE = s·|C−B| = s·BC = s·2√3 = √6 → s = √6/(2√3) = √2/2. So t = 6·(√2/2) = 3√2.\n\nE = (−t−2s, 2√2 s) = (−3√2 − √2, 2√2·√2/2) = (−4√2, 2).\n\nCE = √[(−4√2−1)² + (2−2√2)²] = √[(32+8√2+1) + (4 − 8√2 + 8)] = √[33+8√2 + 12 − 8√2] = √45 = 3√5.",
